# UI consistency before implementation

Before writing or changing user-visible UI, run the **UI consistency** subagent and wait for its reuse report. Do not start the feature until that report exists.

- **Agent:** [ui-consistency-agent.md](../agents/ui-consistency-agent.md)
- **Skill:** [ui-consistency/SKILL.md](../skills/ui-consistency/SKILL.md)

The subagent searches this app and `@webonone/ui-kit` (web) or `@webonone/mobile-ui` (mobile). The implementing agent then follows the report.

## When

Pages, dialogs, lists, forms, controls, empty states, or layout in any `*/frontend`, `ui-kit/`, `mobile/`, or `packages/mobile-ui/`.

Skip backend-only work, migrations, and copy edits that do not change components or layout.

If you **are** the UI consistency agent, do the search and return the report. Do not spawn another copy.

## Order

1. Search for a similar screen or control already in the app or the kit.
2. **Reuse** that component or kit export.
3. When the same markup is copied inline, **extract** it into one component and switch existing call sites first.
4. Only then implement the new feature on that shared piece.

| Used by | Place |
|---------|--------|
| One feature | `features/<module>/components/` |
| Two features, same app | `shared/components/` — [front-end-structure.mdc](front-end-structure.mdc) |
| Two services, or a kit primitive | `@webonone/ui-kit` / `@webonone/mobile-ui` via that agent |

Kit mapping and forbidden raw controls: [ui-kit-consumption.mdc](ui-kit-consumption.mdc). Mobile: [mobile-ui-consumption.mdc](mobile-ui-consumption.mdc).

## Verification

The change summary must include the reuse report (similar UI, component reused or extracted, kit export). Then, in the touched frontend:

```bash
npm run type-check
npm run lint
```
